  "notes": [
    "Pins 1 to 26 of the 40-pin header are electrically the same, so a 26-pin HAT or cape works on a modern Pi. The reverse is not true.",
    "Rev 1 boards (the first Model B, 256 MB) use GPIO0, GPIO1 and GPIO21 where rev 2 and later use GPIO2, GPIO3 and GPIO27. Rev 1 also puts the I2C pins on bus 0 instead of bus 1, so `i2cdetect -y 0` on an old board and `-y 1` on everything since.",
    "Rev 2 boards add a second 8-pin header, P5, that is not on this diagram. It carries GPIO28 to GPIO31 and is unpopulated from the factory.",
    "3.3 V only, like every Pi. A 5 V output into any of these damages the SoC.",
    "GPIO2 and GPIO3 carry fixed 1.8 kOhm pull-ups to 3V3 on the board."
  ],
